## Test Smell Audit — `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1 (.NET 10) | **Scope:** Integration (`[TestCategory("Integration")]`)

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High | 3 | 3 |
| Medium | 1 | 1 |
| Low | 0 | 0 |
| **Total** | **4** | **4** |

---

### Findings by Severity

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Sleepy Test (Smell 3)

**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000); // 3-second hard-coded wait
```

**Why it's bad even for integration tests:** `Thread.Sleep` introduces non-deterministic timing — the event may take longer on slow CI, or the 3 s is wasted overhead when it's ready in 50 ms. This is the #1 predictor of flaky tests (Camara et al., SAST 2021).

**Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    // Poll with timeout instead of sleeping
    var cts = new CancellationTokenSource(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));
    while (!_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
    {
        await Task.Delay(50, cts.Token);
    }

    Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
}
```

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic (Smell 1)

**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 94)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Why:** The `if/else` means one branch is **never exercised** in a given run. The test "passes" regardless of which type is returned, hiding potential regressions.

**Fix — split into explicit typed tests:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandard_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    var user = new User("eve@example.com", "Eve");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremium_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    var user = new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", discountRate: 0.1m);
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com") as PremiumUser;

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test / Unknown Test (Smell 4)

**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)

```csharp
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // No assertion — passes as long as no exception is thrown
}
```

**Why:** This gives false confidence. If `Insert` silently drops rows, or a constraint is violated and swallowed, this test still passes. The name implies a "does-not-throw" intent, but that should be explicit.

**Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette (Extended Catalog)

**Test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Why:** 4 assertions with no message parameters. When one fails in CI, the developer sees only "`Assert.AreEqual failed`" without knowing *which* property was wrong until they read the stack trace line number.

**Fix — add messages (MSTest supports a `message` parameter):**
```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should persist unchanged");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should persist unchanged");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Id should be auto-generated and positive");
```

---

### ✅ Smell-Free Patterns (Well-Written Tests)

| Test | Why it's good |
|------|---------------|
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single clear action → single clear assertion |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count of 3 is contextually obvious (just added 3); uses `CollectionAssert` |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Proper async/await, clear assertion, no sleeps |
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Focused scope, assertions below Roulette threshold |

**General Fixture?** No — both `_connection` and `_repository` are used by every test. Setup is appropriate.

**Mystery Guest?** No — the in-memory SQLite connection (`Data Source=:memory:`) is a hermetic test resource, not an external dependency.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` | 2 min |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | Split into 2 typed tests | 10 min |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with poll loop | 15 min |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | Add message strings to assertions | 5 min |

Fixes 1–3 prevent **silent false-passes** (tests that "pass" while masking real bugs). Fix 4 is a maintainability improvement that pays off in CI triage time.
